                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Wilmington OH",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 10 at 2:53AM EDT until September 10 at 7:00AM EDT by NWS Wilmington OH",
                "description": "At 253 AM EDT, local law enforcement reported flash flooding across\nthe warned area. Between 2.5 and 5.5 inches of rain have fallen.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are possible.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement and local EMA reported significant flooding\noccurring near the Highland County Fairgrounds, with rushing\nwater on SR-73. Additionally, multiple water rescues are\nbeing reported out of Pike County.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban\nareas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\nSome locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nHillsboro, Waverly, Piketon, Marshall, Bainbridge, Kincaid Springs,\nCynthiana, Pike Lake, Highland Holiday, Rocky Fork Point, Russell,\nNew Market, Beaver, Sinking Spring, Idaho, Elm Grove, Buchanan,\nRainsboro, Summithill and Rocky Fork Lake.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nTo report flash flooding, go to our website at weather.gov/iln and\nsubmit your report via social media, when you can do so safely.",
